# Who must approve a change to what.
#
# DELIBERATELY INERT while this repository has one contributor. GitHub never
# requests a review from the author of a pull request, so with a single
# maintainer every rule below would either do nothing or, combined with
# "Require review from Code Owners", lock the only person out of their own
# repository. CONTRIBUTING.md makes the same point about review in general:
# self-merging is a consequence of the head count and expires with it.
#
# The ownership map is worth writing down now anyway — it is the part that takes
# thought, and it is the same map whether or not it is enforced yet.
#
# TO ACTIVATE, when the second person gets write access:
#   1. Replace @Trade-Ties/maintainers with a real GitHub team or user. An
#      owner without write access to this repository makes the entry invalid,
#      and GitHub applies it silently as if it were not there.
#   2. Uncomment the rules.
#   3. In the main ruleset, set required approvals to 1 and turn on
#      "Require review from Code Owners".
#
# Last match wins — order matters, most specific goes last.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
# *                     @Trade-Ties/maintainers

# The API contract. The one file both builds read, and the only place where a
# careless edit breaks the frontend and the backend at the same time. This is
# the highest-value line in the file — everything else is ordinary code.
# /api/                 @Trade-Ties/maintainers

# /backend/             @Trade-Ties/maintainers
# /frontend/            @Trade-Ties/maintainers

# Deployment topology, TLS termination and the record of what a deployment
# needs. A mistake here is not caught by any test.
# /infra/               @Trade-Ties/maintainers

# The rules themselves: CI, branch rulesets, the commit hook, and the documents
# that describe how code reaches customers. Changing these changes every future
# change.
# /.github/             @Trade-Ties/maintainers
# /.githooks/           @Trade-Ties/maintainers
# /CONTRIBUTING.md      @Trade-Ties/maintainers
# /BRANCHING.md         @Trade-Ties/maintainers
